{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"damaged-plaster-loris","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTwo epic siblings need live measurements this shared host cannot make: the sentinel story must\nshow before/after raw-output distributions (the directive itself changes what models emit —\nmeasured E2: quote-in-prose 0% -> 100%), and the capability-rows story needs per-cell\nPASS/FAIL facts for direct-Anthropic and OpenAI cells. The API keys live only in CI\n(.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:118-119 scopes ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY\nper matrix provider arm), budget is limited, and keys must not be exposed to clients on shared\nhosts — so measurement runs belong in a manual, capped CI job (operator decision recorded on\nthe epic).\n\n## Approach\n\nA harness under tests/external/ (the live-call convention, e.g. alongside\ntests/external/_live_llm.py) parameterized from `.github/llm-providers/*.toml` (anthropic,\nbedrock, openai): for each (provider, model) cell and each directive variant (current vs\nsentinel), run a fixed n=10 of two production-shaped prompts (the df3a-shaped agentic\ntranscript with a quoted dep record, and a single-shot contract step), capture every raw reply\nas an artifact file, and score deterministically: parse success under the current parser vs\nthe new selection+sentinel parser, and layout-class rates (prose, fenced, multi-object,\nquoted-JSON). A new `workflow_dispatch`-only job (in external-integration.yml or a sibling\nworkflow reusing its per-provider secret scoping) uploads the artifact bundle; a\nworkflow-input call cap (default 300 calls/run) is enforced in the harness before any call.\nCells whose key is absent are recorded \"unmeasured\" and skipped without failing the job. The\ncommitted E2 replies serve as the scorer's golden fixtures, so the scoring logic is fully\ntestable offline.\n\n## Scope\n\n- tests/external/ (new harness module) — cells, prompts, capture, scoring, cap\n- .github/workflows/ (the dispatch job) — secret scoping copied from the existing per-provider\n  matrix arms\n- tests/unit/ (new scorer test file) — golden-count tests on committed fixtures\n- tests/fixtures/ — E2 reply corpus committed as scorer goldens\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier for everything deterministic (the live boundary is the only mock-free external):\n\n- Scorer reproduces the E2 golden counts on the committed fixture replies (exact numbers\n  pinned).\n- Credential-absent cell -> recorded \"unmeasured\", exit 0 (skip path is python logic, not\n  YAML, so it is unit-testable).\n- Call-budget cap: a matrix exceeding the cap refuses to start (asserted before any network\n  object is constructed).\n- The live run itself is operator-triggered and its evidence is the uploaded artifact — per\n  the shared test-design standard §10, scored deterministically with predeclared n and\n  thresholds; CI never gates on live-model nondeterminism.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Scorer golden tests pass on the committed E2 fixtures — checked by the new unit tests\n      under `make test`.\n- [ ] Missing-credential cells record \"unmeasured\" without failing — checked by the skip-path\n      unit test.\n- [ ] The per-run call budget is enforced and predeclared as a workflow input — checked by the\n      cap unit test plus the input's presence in the workflow file.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] One workflow_dispatch run completes and its artifact (raw replies +\n      before/after score table) is linked as a comment on this ticket.","id":"a40f-25e4-885c-4cca","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Provider-matrix raw-output baseline eval harness in CI"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785891888589945001,"uuid":"6c30e7b6-8d26-4238-8de0-e7f919b3d572"}